{"ts":"2026-07-06T08:03:09.588Z","author":"maintainer-agent","op":"create","patch":[{"op":"replace","path":"/body","value":"GitHub: https://github.com/unbraind/pm-cli/issues/450\n\n## Problem (silent wrong data)\n`--duration 5m` on meet/event/remind parses as 5 MONTHS (relative-parser: m=months, PR#263 decision; minutes = `5min`, added by pm-zoe4). Help shows only 1h/2d examples and never warns; a \"5-minute standup\" silently becomes a 5-month meeting with warnings: []. Every mainstream scheduling convention treats m=minutes.\n\n## Proposed fix (needs a small decision)\nOptions: (a) flip `m` to minutes with `mo` for months (breaking but convention-aligned; alias window + warning); (b) make bare `m` ambiguous -> hard error suggesting `min`/`mo`; (c) keep semantics but emit a loud warning + document. Recommend (b) then (a) after a deprecation cycle. Record choice on ADR log (pm-m2u1).\n\n## Definition of done\n`--duration 5m` can no longer silently produce months; help/docs document duration units exhaustively; parser spec covers m/min/mo; migration note in changelog item."},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/id","value":"pm-jkjt"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/title","value":"GH-450: --duration 5m parses as 5 MONTHS — silent wrong data on meet/event/remind"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/description","value":"Dogfood GH-450: relative-parser maps m=months (PR#263) so a 5-minute standup becomes a 5-month meeting with no warning; minutes exist as 'min' (pm-zoe4). Needs an ambiguity guard or convention flip. Duplicate check: pm-zoe4 (closed) added min granularity only; pm-o3fh moves the shortcuts but not the parser; no open overlap."},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/type","value":"Issue"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/status","value":"open"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/priority","value":1},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/tags","value":["agent-ux","bug","calendar","gh-issue"]},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/created_at","value":"2026-07-06T08:03:09.588Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-07-06T08:03:09.588Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/author","value":"maintainer-agent"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/estimated_minutes","value":90},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/acceptance_criteria","value":"Bare 'm' duration can no longer silently mean months (error-with-hint or convention flip with deprecation window, decision recorded under pm-m2u1); duration units exhaustively documented; parser spec covers m/min/mo"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/parent","value":"pm-mpbb"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/risk","value":"medium"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/confidence","value":"high"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/dependencies","value":[{"id":"pm-o3fh","kind":"related","created_at":"2026-07-06T08:03:09.588Z"}]}],"before_hash":"3cc22dff72be7b14824654a7a64ea62b04799939b2fee54c1b5f52ca60bf6df0","after_hash":"0d5b64af688f96b4ab5545a654a46ae87df66d39a7da694a7b73425e4bac7350","message":""}
